A client confirms the handshake on an acknowledgement of a 1-RTT packet, as quic-go does.

quic-go's handleAckFrame, when the ACK it has just processed acknowledged a 1-RTT packet — which
it can only have done in a 1-RTT packet — confirms the handshake on the client side at once
(vendor/quic-go/connection.go:2150-2166, acked1RTTPacket from
vendor/quic-go/internal/ackhandler/sent_packet_handler.go:467-478), as RFC 9001 section 4.1.2
allows, rather than waiting for HANDSHAKE_DONE. Confirming drops the Handshake keys and ends
whatever the client still had to send in that space. ngtcp2 waits for HANDSHAKE_DONE, so a lost
one left the client in the Handshake space for a round trip or more where the reference was not.

diff --git a/lib/ngtcp2_conn.c b/lib/ngtcp2_conn.c
--- a/lib/ngtcp2_conn.c
+++ b/lib/ngtcp2_conn.c
@@ -6869,6 +6869,8 @@
  * NGTCP2_ERR_CALLBACK_FAILURE
  *     User callback failed.
  */
+static int conn_recv_handshake_done(ngtcp2_conn *conn, ngtcp2_tstamp ts);
+
 static int conn_recv_ack(ngtcp2_conn *conn, ngtcp2_pktns *pktns, ngtcp2_ack *fr,
                          ngtcp2_tstamp pkt_ts, ngtcp2_tstamp ts) {
   ngtcp2_ssize num_acked;
@@ -6901,6 +6903,17 @@
 
   ngtcp2_conn_set_loss_detection_timer(conn, ts);
 
+  /* A client takes an ACK of one of its 1-RTT packets, arriving in a
+     1-RTT packet, as the handshake confirmed, without waiting for
+     HANDSHAKE_DONE: quic-go's handleAckFrame, from acked1RTTPacket
+     (vendor/quic-go/connection.go:2150-2166,
+     vendor/quic-go/internal/ackhandler/sent_packet_handler.go:467-478),
+     RFC 9001 section 4.1.2. */
+  if (!conn->server && pktns == &conn->pktns &&
+      !(conn->flags & NGTCP2_CONN_FLAG_HANDSHAKE_CONFIRMED)) {
+    return conn_recv_handshake_done(conn, ts);
+  }
+
   return 0;
 }
 
